Three findings from the audit (notes/audit-report.md; plan and adversarial
review in notes/batch2-guide.md), all instances of one root cause: capability
lists survive on the paths built for them, and vanish wherever machinery that
predates the feature rebuilds a type or a callee expression.

MF1: a property accessor's 'throws' clause was enforced inside the accessor but
demanded nothing at use sites, because the desugared callee expression was given
a capability-free functional type. All three desugar sites (get, set, and the
compound-assignment getter) now carry the accessor's list, instantiated through
the RECEIVER's type so an inherited or extended generic accessor demands
'MyExc<Int64>' rather than a bare 'MyExc<T>'. A defensive fallback in HandleCall
recovers the declared clause whenever a callee expression carries none.

MF6: a primary constructor's clause was parsed and then discarded by
DesugarPrimaryCtor, so construction sites demanded nothing, the clause was never
validated, and a public primary constructor got a spurious error in its own
body — the proposal's own 3.2 example did not compile. The clause is now cloned
onto the synthesized 'init'.

MF2 (part): inferred lists are written into declaration types between inference
and checking (CompleteInferredCapabilityTypes), so a declaration's own type is
the single source of its list. Expression types are deliberately NOT completed:
they were formed during type check, so re-typing them would double-charge call
sites, which read the inference map instead. The remaining half of MF2
(demanding at function-value formation) is left open — the adversarial review
disproved its premise; see notes/batch2-guide.md section 5.

Also fixed, found by the review rather than reported: neither hand-written
ThrowsClause copier (ASTCloner, PartialInstantiation) carried the '...' marker,
so a cloned declaration could silently flip between inference-eligible and not.

Tests: property accessors demanded at read/write/compound-assign/increment sites
and their positive twin; generic accessor instantiation, positive and negative;
primary constructors with clauses incl. struct form, 'throws ()' and a field
initializer discharged by the constructor's clause.

Gate: CheckedExceptions 56/64 (the 8 failures are the three features not yet
implemented); ctest 49/49; Parser/Sema LLT 3934/3934; clang-format clean.

